macOS

### Operating System Version

Sequoia 15.5

### What arch are you using?

x64

### Last Known Working Electron version

36.7.3

### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?

I don't know

### Expected Behavior

After upgrading from Electron 36.7.3 → 37.2.4, all HTML5 media (e.g. MP4) reports .duration === 0 and immediately emits the ended event. Downgrading back to 36.7.3 restores correct behavior. This breaks any logic that waits for a real duration or playback to complete.

### Actual Behavior

Opened `<video>` immediately emits the ended event.

### Testcase Gist URL

_No response_

### Additional Information

Minimal Example

```js
// main.js
const { app, BrowserWindow } = require('electron');
app.whenReady().then(() => {
  const win = new BrowserWindow({ webPreferences: { nodeIntegration: true } });
  win.loadFile('index.html');
});
```

```html
<!-- index.html -->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><meta charset="utf-8"></head>
<body>
  <video id="video" src="file:///absolute/path/to/video.mp4" controls autoplay></video>
  <script>
    const v = document.getElementById('video');
    v.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', () => {
      console.log('duration:', v.duration);
    });
    v.addEventListener('ended', () => {
      console.warn('ended event fired');
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

